vLLM #65282 (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/65282; first #63350), backported to v0.33.0.

The scheduler.py part of these commits on vLLM v0.33.0 (4ba787ec9):

  b0b339e57 [Core] Priority scheduling: preempt lower-priority requests for KV cache space (cherry-picked from 7f048ee9e)
    Backport: v0.33.0's SchedulerStats and Prometheus logger have no field
    for the preemptions, so the scheduler counts them and make_stats leaves
    them; and v0.33.0's waiting loop bounds a prefix cache hit by the aux-
    output connector alone, so make-room does too, and the test of main's
    prompt-scoring bound is left out; and v0.33.0 has no queue of requests
    waiting to start an async KV load (main's async_kv_waiting), so
    make-room's target scan and the in-flight gate cover its two waiting
    queues, the gate testing request_queue is self.waiting, with the tests
    of that queue left out, and its KV cache blocks hold their pool, not a
    weak reference to it, so the released-blocks count compares the pool
    itself.

